  "surface": "backend",
  "riskClass": "medium",
  "title": "supplier-service CSV product upload silently skips conflicts with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING — no error count returned to caller",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: business_logic. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The CSV bulk upload endpoint for supplier products uses `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` (approximately line 731) when inserting products in batches of 100. When a conflict occurs (e.g., duplicate barcode or SKU), the row is silently skipped. The API response does not differentiate between successfully inserted rows and skipped conflicts. A supplier uploading 500 products where 200 have duplicate barcodes would see '500 processed' without knowing 200 were skipped. This can lead to confusion about which products were actually added and which need manual correction.",
  "status": "done",
  "severity": "P2",
